  "reviewNotes": "PDF page5 and native front/back/cutaway-top/direct-front source views. Source860010 triangles, maximum86.425003mm and native datum17mm. Comparison of six measured frame-head points with MT1-028 finds median distance.274mm for\u221290deg versus1.237mm for+90deg, confirming rotated frame orientation independently of the positiveX counter. Eight new frame heads have source ray intersections. Lower and middle braces meet different rear joints[12.14,42.3]/[12.14,47.39]mm; front joints[-9.69,30.46]/[-9.69,59.22]mm. Countertop source rays32.96111\u201333.88136mm. Tray axes\u2212.75/2.25deg come from side-normal histograms and independent projected bounds. Measured upper fruit caps at39.5mm seed warm red tones, matching author reference; the carrot tray has horizontal roots and its own orange material. Narrow fruit/root interiors protect wooden rails. No tablecloth or liquid is present. Canopy protects posts, caps and braces. Free left paving[-10,0,25.787424]mm gives stand point[.214286,.5]; positiveX counter and north/south frame strips are blocked. Review canopy/timber boundaries, fruit rails, root interiors and both tiers before publication. Compact render packing at768px detected a physical UV collision of.247mm, despite the1024px pass. Recreate the render UV at.5rad with.0025 margin and rebake before publication. Close cutaway views identify fruit back rail at39.4\u201339.8mm and carrot wooden floor near36.1mm. Exclude the rear rail strip aboveY10.7 up to39.9mm from red pigment; start carrot pigment at36.6mm and stop its back edge atY\u22123.0. Increase LOD island margin to.003 to separate contrasting cloth and tiny timber UV islands.",
